+The named `IAMService` HTTP client uses the accepted Defaults `AddLegacyIamServiceAuthentication` handler and its separate IAM-profile token provider. Accounting's outgoing live-check request requires that profile; an unavailable profile fails with 503 before network access, without trying the general legacy token provider. Its origin validation, redirect prohibition, credential-header redaction and ten-second timeout remain intact.
+
+General downstream Accounting clients and financial-ownership read requests retain their legacy-audience token composition. This change supplies Accounting's own outbound IAM admission token; it does not add a GUID claim to a financial reader token, resolve a managed workload principal, register a catalogue entry or create a binding.
+
+All 22 Accounting workflow Defaults checkouts and the structural pin assertions now target independently accepted `7b3099bf67d0f17e56cfdb3dcf36541304abaac2`. Two source-authored tests inspect the actual Accounting registered handler chain and exercise missing IAM-profile admission with zero physical network calls and no general-provider fallback. Their execution is pending; main Accounting forecast is 1655, employee subset remains 169 and the separate ordinary-principal project remains 23. Existing full native coverage and static gates are retained.
+
+Required server configuration and actual normal Auth enrollment are separate owner inputs. This source slice does not supply credentials, invent principal mappings, apply grants, or establish the complete live financial join. Build, two focused composition tests, the full affected Accounting suite, all four generated-inclusive coverage gates, formatting, vulnerability/secret checks and protected hosted validation are mandatory before publication.
diff --git a/docs/financial-caller-replay-isolation.md b/docs/financial-caller-replay-isolation.md
