--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/financial-caller-replay-isolation.md
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+# Financial create replay identity isolation
+
+The normal generic create route previously looked up a replay memo by resource scope and SHA256(Idempotency-Key) only. Separate authenticated callers using the same key could therefore receive the same invoice, receipt, payment or catalogue response. The source135e financial controllers did not define this replay feature; this correction repairs isolation of the target adaptation while preserving their scalar and route contracts.
+
+CrudController now binds keyed creates to exactly one authenticated issuer and subject (with the standard mapped NameIdentifier fallback). It hashes a JSON-framed issuer/subject pair into a versioned resource scope. The existing Redis adapter continues to hash the caller's key and retain the 24-hour response. Raw identity fields are not stored in the key, and old unbound memo keys are never read or migrated. Missing/ambiguous identity refuses the keyed write before the memo or repository is called. Same-caller replay remains response-stable even when a later body differs; missing/blank idempotency keys retain ordinary create behavior.
+
+Sixteen authored regression cases cover normal HTTP/JWT/live-permission/owned Redis creates across seven resources (Accounts, Directions, Methods, Types, Payments, Invoices, Receipts), each caller's stable replay, old unbound memo decoys and missing/ambiguous identity before store access. The retained source mutation oracle computes expected keys independently from the fixture JWT. These cases are forecasts, not native passes. This combined successor retains all16 replay cases plus the source-cleared IAM44/ordinary-principal inputs. Main forecast is1671 and employee169; separately built ordinary-principal/catalogue/cleanup forecast remains23. Both predecessor packets are preserved. Source integration is not native acceptance.
+
+Build, focused/full native tests, raw coverage, format/analyzer/audit checks and owned runtime cleanup verification remain pending admission. No live data/schema, grant, provider or deployment change is authorized by this draft. This slice does not add concurrent same-caller exclusion or durable response recovery after a Redis outage; those remain separate behavior limits.
diff --git a/provisioning/iam/README.md b/provisioning/iam/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..17722f6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/provisioning/iam/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+The Accounting financial ownership reader owns `legacy.accounting-financial-ownership.read` with catalogue service `legacy`, resource `accounting-financial-ownership` and action `read`. The old four-segment permission is rejected by ordinary IAM registration and by the Accounting HTTP controls.
+
+`scripts/Register-AccountingFinancialOwnershipPermission.ps1` explicitly provisions the checked-in request through the existing IAM `POST /iam/v1/permissions/register` endpoint. A separately authorized operator supplies the HTTPS IAM origin and a secure token with the endpoint's existing `iam.permissions.create` authority. The script refuses redirects, uses a 30-second timeout, verifies the returned catalogue tuple and releases HTTP resources. It is never invoked by application startup. No message-bus publisher is registered.
+
+Catalogue registration does not create roles, principals or bindings. Auth and Quotation token composition and ordinary resource-scoped binding to actual persisted GUID IAM principals are separate owner boundaries. Unknown opaque subjects must fail closed. No live provisioning or grants were executed for this draft.
+
+`tooling/Accounting.PermissionRegistration.Tests` references the actual IAM Application project using an explicit `IamServiceSourceRoot`; it calls `PermissionService.RegisterPermissionsAsync` with the same JSON request and asserts catalogue fields, mismatched service rejection and rejection of the predecessor permission. Repository and event transport are mocked: these tests do not prove persisted principal binding or live permission checks. Reviewed IAM source head: `4fe6642e5674013de9a3672505aec898fdcae0ed`.
+
+Native build and tests remain on hold. Required qualification is a zero-warning Release build, this four-case catalogue boundary suite, the existing Accounting HTTP regression and full suite, formatting, vulnerability and secret checks, followed by real enrolled-principal/scoped-binding end-to-end verification coordinated with Auth, IAM and AppHost. No commit or publication precedes those applicable gates.
